WEBVTT

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.883
&GT;&GT; SENATE COMMITTEE ON LABOR,
PUBLIC EMPLOYMENT

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.785
AND RETIREMENT WILL BEGIN.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.122
AND WE ARE GOING TO START AS A
SUBCOMMITTEE TODAY.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.124
I SEE SOME OF THE MEMBERS ARE
HERE,

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.626
AND WE WILL START OUT OF FILE

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.230
ORDER WITH ITEM NUMBER 13 AB

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:33.299
2975 ASSEMBLY MEMBER GIBSON.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.402
PLEASE COME FORWARD.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.741
PROCEED WHEN READY.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:47.680
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU VERY MUCH, MADAM
CHAIR AND MEMBERS.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:50.083
FIRST OF ALL, I WANT TO SAY
THANK YOU VERY MUCH

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.319
FOR ALLOWING ME TO PRESENT
ASSEMBLY BILL 2975.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.189
I WANT TO START OFF BY ACCEPTING

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:59.159
THE THE THE COMMITTEE
AMENDMENTS.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.927
I WANT TO THANK THE CHAIR AND
THE STAFF FOR WORKING

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:05.532
WITH US TO STRENGTHENING, UM,
ASSEMBLY BILL 2975.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.233
I BELIEVE THIS BILL IS A VERY

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.469
COMMON SENSE BILL ABOUT, UM,

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.404
PROTECTING OUR HOSPITAL,

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.206
MAKING SURE THAT OUR FRONTLINE
WORKERS,

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.208
AS WELL AS OUR PATIENTS,

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.976
WHO'S GOING TO THESE HOSPITALS,

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.845
HAVE A SAFE ENVIRONMENT.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.815
AND SO THIS BILL SEEKS TO
IMPROVE THE HOSPITAL

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.584
SAFETY BY REQUIRING WEAPONS
DETECTING

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:28.354
SCREENINGS AT SELECTED HOSPITAL
ENTRANCES

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.690
CONDUCTED BY TRAINED PERSONNEL.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.926
ACCORDING TO THE UNITED STATES

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.828
BUREAU OF LABOR STATISTICS,

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:38.598
HEALTH CARE WORKERS ARE FIVE
TIMES MORE LIKELY

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:41.935
TO SUFFER WORKPLACE INJURIES
OR VIOLENCE,

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.038
AND WORKERS THAN WORKERS
OVERALL,

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:48.475
AND VIOLENCE IS TRENDING UPWARD

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.610
IN OUR HEALTH CARE FACILITIES.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.413
THIS BILL, ASSEMBLY BILL 2975,

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.349
PROPOSES TO ENHANCE THE
REQUIREMENT OF

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:59.619
SAFETY MEASURES FOR HOSPITALS BY

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.788
REQUIRING COMMON SENSE MEASURES,

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.556
SUCH AS WEAPON DETECTION,

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:07.961
SCREENINGS AT SELECTIVE
ENTRANCES TO ENSURE

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.497
HOSPITALS REMAIN SAFE AND PLACE,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.999
HEALING UM, AND NOT VIOLENCE.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:13.900
AT THE FOREFRONT.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.235
WITH ME TO PROVIDE SUPPORTING

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.237
TESTIMONY IS MICHELLE HAMM,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:22.509
UM, A KAISER, UH, WORKER, AND
ALSO, UM, FIONA, UH,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.711
WHO'S A NURSE AT THE LOS ANGELES
COUNTY,

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:25.945
UM, MEDICAL CENTER,

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.481
A COUNTY HOSPITAL WILL ALSO SELF
INTRODUCE

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.250
WHO ARE MY LEAD WITNESSES.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.953
WE'LL HAVE THE WITNESSES AT THE
PODIUM

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.488
AND YOU HAVE TWO MINUTES.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:35.855
&GT;&GT; ALL RIGHT.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.489
THANK YOU.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.790
MY NAME IS MICHELLE HORN.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.958
I'VE BEEN A REGISTERED NURSE IN

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.126
THE PACKAGE UNIT AT KAISER

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.695
PERMANENTE MORENO VALLEY
HOSPITAL FOR TEN YEARS.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.398
I ALSO HAVE SEVEN YEARS OF
EXPERIENCE AS AN E.R.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.933
NURSE AT OTHER HOSPITALS.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.435
SO I HAVE A DEEP UNDERSTANDING
OF THE MANY WORKPLACE

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.539
HAZARDS THAT NURSES FACE ON THE
JOB AT ANY HOSPITAL.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.741
OF THE LONG LIST OF DANGERS THAT
NURSES

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.609
AND OTHER HEALTH CARE WORKERS
FACE DAILY,

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.411
THE POSSIBILITY OF AN
ENCOUNTERING

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.013
AN EMOTIONALLY CHARGED PATIENT

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.948
OR VISITOR WIELDING A DANGEROUS

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.683
WEAPON IS THE MOST TERRIFYING.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.119
IT IS A VERY REAL THREAT TO OUR
SAFETY,

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.888
BUT IT IS ALSO ONE OF THE
EASIEST TO PREVENT.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.891
CURRENTLY, THERE IS NO SINGLE
STATEWIDE POLICY

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.893
OR STANDARD TO ADDRESS THIS
THREAT.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.461
INSTEAD, WE HAVE A PATCHWORK OF

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.496
DIFFERENT POLICIES DEVELOPED

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:19.365
BY INDIVIDUAL HOSPITALS AT THEIR
OWN DISCRETION.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.868
THAT IS NO WAY TO DEAL WITH SUCH
A PERVASIVE

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.603
AND LIFE THREATENING PROBLEM.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:27.674
IN 2022, TWO NURSES AND A DOCTOR
WERE STABBED

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.543
AND IN ENCINO MEDICAL CENTER IN

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.612
LOS ANGELES BY A PATIENT WHO
ENTERED

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.814
THE HOSPITAL WITH A CONCEALED
KNIFE.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.950
IT MAY BE THE MOST NOTORIOUS
EXAMPLE

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.851
OF HOSPITAL VIOLENCE IN OUR
AREA,

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.520
BUT IT COULD HAVE HAPPENED
ANYWHERE.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:43.556
WE ARE URGING YOU TO PASS AB
2975

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.258
SO THAT IT NEVER HAPPENS AGAIN.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.660
BY REQUIRING METAL DETECTORS,

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.896
TRAINED METAL DETECTORS STAFFED

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.765
BY TRAINED SECURITY OFFICERS AT
EVERY HOSPITAL,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.634
WE CAN PROTECT PATIENTS AND
PROVIDE THEM WITH

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.337
CARE WITHOUT FEARING FOR OUR
OWN SAFETY.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.473
FEAR IS WHAT I FELT WHEN A
PATIENT'S

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.375
INTOXICATED HUSBAND GOT IN MY
FACE

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.210
AND THREATENED ME WHILE HIS WIFE

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.812
WAS EXPERIENCING A MISCARRIAGE.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.614
WE WERE WORKING TO ENSURE THAT
SHE DIDN'T

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.716
SUFFER ADDITIONAL COMPLICATIONS,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.418
BUT HE WAS INCREASINGLY ERRATIC
AND IRRATIONAL,

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:13.920
BLAMING THE HOSPITAL STAFF

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:16.022
AND EVERYONE ELSE FOR HIS LOSS.

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:19.025
I KNEW HE COULD LASH OUT IN THE
STATE HE WAS IN,

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.060
BUT OUR HOSPITAL DID NOT HAVE
A POLICY

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.229
TO KEEP HIM FROM BRINGING IN
A WEAPON,

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.131
AND THAT SCARED ME THE MOST.

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:26.666
THAT WAS THE FIRST TIME I ASKED

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.001
SECURITY OFFICERS TO ESCORT

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:31.237
ME TO MY CAR AFTER MY SHIFT, BUT
NOT THE LAST.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.406
ALL HEALTH CARE WORKERS SHOULD
BE

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.241
ABLE TO FOCUS ON PROVIDING CARE,

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.844
NOT LOCATING THE THE NEAREST
EXIT

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.078
OR WHAT THEY COULD USE TO DEFEND

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.114
THEMSELVES IN CASE THEY'RE
ATTACKED

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.316
OR TO PROTECT OUR PATIENTS.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:47.220
AB 2975 WILL MAKE OUR HOSPITAL
SAFER,

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.589
WHICH MEANS OUR PATIENTS WILL
GET BETTER CARE.

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:50.757
I URGE YOU TO SUPPORT IT.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.457
THANK YOU.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:52.492
THANK YOU.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.161
ARE THERE ANY OTHER WITNESSES
SPEAKING

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.062
IN SUPPORT OF THE BILL?

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.764
PLEASE STEP FORWARD.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.731
GOOD AFTERNOON.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.166
HI, MY NAME IS FIONA HANNON.

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:02.802
I AM A REGISTERED NURSE AT LA
COUNTY MEDICAL CENTER.

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:04.937
WE'VE JUST CHANGED OUR NAME TO
LA GENERAL,

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.674
SO I'VE BEEN THERE FOR 25 YEARS.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.043
RIGHT BEFORE I STARTED, THERE
WERE THREE

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.878
DOCTORS THAT WERE SHOT IN OUR
EMERGENCY

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.947
ROOM BECAUSE A PATIENT WANTED
PAIN MEDICATION

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.683
AND THOUGHT THE WAIT WAS TOO
LONG.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:19.352
SO I FEEL COMFORTABLE GOING
TO WORK

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.487
EVERY DAY KNOWING THAT NOW,

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.289
OUR HOSPITAL USED COMMON SENSE

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:25.324
AND IT DOES HAVE METAL DETECTION

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:28.061
SYSTEM THERE WHERE WE JUST WALK
THROUGH THE DOORS.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.729
IT DOESN'T SLOW EVERYTHING DOWN
BECAUSE

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.130
YOU JUST WALK RIGHT THROUGH.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.299
SO WE FEEL SAFE GOING TO WORK.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.001
A LOT OF TIMES YOU DO HAVE
PATIENTS

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:36.436
WITH MENTAL HEALTH ISSUES.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.104
YOU HAVE JUST GENERAL PEOPLE

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.272
WITH MENTAL HEALTH ISSUES.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.074
WE'RE IN AN AREA WHERE YOU HAVE
GANGS.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.842
YOU DON'T KNOW WHAT TYPE OF
WEAPONS COME IN.

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:44.744
THEY RETRIEVE SOME WEAPONS
THROUGH THE E.R.,

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.245
BUT THEY DON'T GET EVERYTHING.

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.548
THIS IS A WAY TO ENSURE THAT
EVERYONE'S

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.316
GOING TO BE SAFE AGAIN.

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:52.785
PATIENT SAFETY IS OUR NUMBER ONE

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.455
STAFF SAFETY IS OUR NUMBER ONE.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.523
WE SHOULDN'T HAVE TO FEAR GOING
TO

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.125
WORK TO TAKE CARE OF OTHER
PEOPLE,

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.359
SAVING LIVES, KNOWING THAT OUR

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.761
LIVES COULD BE IN JEOPARDY.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:07.066
SO I AM DEFINITELY IN SUPPORT
OF AB 2975.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.502
I THINK, UM, THEY SHOULD BE

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:10.770
INSTALLED AT ALL HOSPITALS.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.305
I'M SAD SADDENED TO SEE THAT

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.340
THE PREVIOUS NURSE DOESN'T HAVE
ANY,

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.976
UH, COMING INTO THIS BUILDING.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.978
WE WENT THROUGH METAL DETECTION,

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.480
I WENT THROUGH THE AIRPORT,

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:21.848
WE GO THROUGH METAL DETECTION.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.082
EVERYWHERE YOU GO, YOU HAVE IT.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:25.785
EVEN BASIC CONCERTS, YOU CAN'T.

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:27.620
YOU HAVE TO CARRY SEE THROUGH
BAGS.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.055
WE DON'T HAVE ANY OF THAT.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:32.859
SO THAT'S ANOTHER FAIL SAFE STEP
FOR EVERYONE

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.660
TO FEEL SAFE COMING INTO OUR
BUILDINGS.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.897
AND I THINK IT NEEDS TO BE IN
EVERY SINGLE HOSPITAL.

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:40.066
THANK YOU FOR TAKING THE TIME
TO LISTEN TO ME.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.134
THANK YOU.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.636
OKAY, NOW WE'LL HAVE WITNESSES.

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:45.104
UH, NOT WITNESSES, BUT FOLKS
WHO WANT

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.372
TO SPEAK IN SUPPORT OF THIS
BILL.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.473
PLEASE STEP FORWARD.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.343
STATE YOUR NAME, AFFILIATION
AND POSITION.

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:54.914
&GT;&GT; GOOD AFTERNOON, MADAM CHAIR
YVONNE FERNANDEZ WITH

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:56.716
THE CALIFORNIA LABOR FEDERATION
IN SUPPORT.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:00.620
&GT;&GT; OKAY.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:01.554
SEEING NO OTHER WITNESSES,

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:02.989
WE WILL MOVE TO OPPOSITION.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:05.191
IS THEIR WITNESS?

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:05.591
OKAY.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:06.192
WITNESSES.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:07.426
YOU EACH HAVE TWO MINUTES.

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:08.127
&GT;&GT; APPRECIATE IT.

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.296
CHAIR, SENATORS, COMMITTEE
STAFF.

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:11.430
I'LL BE BRIEF.

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:13.466
MY NAME IS DEAN GRIFFITH WITH
CAPITAL ADVOCACY HERE

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.968
ON BEHALF OF THE CALIFORNIA
HOSPITAL ASSOCIATION.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:20.339
WE REMAIN IN RESPECTFUL
OPPOSITION TO AB 2975.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.875
PATIENT AND EMPLOYEE SAFETY WILL
ALWAYS

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:25.411
BE A TOP PRIORITY FOR OUR
HOSPITALS.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.847
WHILE WE'RE STILL REVIEWING
THESE RECENT AMENDMENTS,

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:29.782
WHICH MAKE A VERY SIGNIFICANT
STEP

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:30.983
AND ABSOLUTELY APPRECIATE

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.185
THE HARD WORK BY ASSEMBLY MEMBER

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:34.020
GIBSON AND HIS TEAM,

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:36.689
MADAM CHAIR AND COMMITTEE STAFF
PEREZ.

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:39.525
AND THE BILL SPONSOR.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:40.960
CALIFORNIA.

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:42.595
SEIU CALIFORNIA.

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:45.264
WE LOOK FORWARD TO CONTINUING
TO WORK WITH ALL,

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:48.601
ALL TOWARDS A CREATIVE SOLUTION
ON THAT SHARED

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:51.404
PRIORITY OF PATIENT AND EMPLOYEE
SAFETY.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.104
THANK YOU.

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:57.276
&GT;&GT; UH, THANK YOU, MADAM CHAIR

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:58.644
AND COMMITTEE MEMBER SARAH
BRIDGE,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:07:59.946
ON BEHALF OF THE ASSOCIATION OF

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:01.314
CALIFORNIA HEALTHCARE DISTRICTS

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.349
HERE RESPECTFULLY OPPOSE, UNLESS
AMENDED,

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:05.451
TO AB 2975.

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.887
HD REPRESENTS THE 77 PUBLIC
HEALTH CARE

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:09.288
DISTRICTS THROUGHOUT THE STATE,

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:12.358
OVER HALF OF WHICH OWN AND OR
OPERATE A HOSPITAL.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:13.993
I WANT TO FIRST THANK THE
AUTHOR,

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.695
SPONSORS AND COMMITTEE STAFF
FOR THEIR

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.330
CONTINUED WORK ON THE BILL.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:18.497
WE FEEL LIKE THE BILL IS MOVING

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:19.532
IN A POSITIVE DIRECTION.

00:08:19.599 --> 00:08:21.434
HOWEVER, AT THIS TIME WE HAVE
REMAINED

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.902
CONCERNS ABOUT THE
IMPLEMENTATION

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:24.036
OF THE BILL AND THE POTENTIAL

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:25.605
LIABILITIES IT CREATES.

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:28.107
DISTRICT HOSPITALS PRIORITY AND
PRIMARY CONCERN

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:30.376
IS THE SAFETY OF OUR STAFF AND
PATIENTS.

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:32.511
IT IS FOR THOSE REASONS, WE WANT
TO ENSURE

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:33.846
THAT THE SHARED GOAL OF MAKING

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:35.548
HOSPITALS A SAFER PLACE CAN
ACTUALLY

00:08:35.615 --> 00:08:37.049
BE ACHIEVED THROUGH THE BILL.

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:38.751
AS MENTIONED IN THE ANALYSIS,

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:40.953
HOSPITALS ARE FEDERALLY REQUIRED
TO PROVIDE

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.755
ACCESS TO CARE FOR ALL PATIENTS
SEEKING

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:44.824
HOSPITAL AND EMERGENCY SERVICES.

00:08:44.891 --> 00:08:46.392
THERE ARE CURRENTLY NO FEDERAL

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:47.493
OR STATE STATUTES ALLOWING

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.295
A HOSPITAL TO REJECT AN
INDIVIDUAL

00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:50.663
WHO IS SEEKING CARE,

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:51.864
BECAUSE THEY HAVE AN ITEM THAT

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.165
MAY CONSTITUTE A WEAPON.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:55.368
FURTHER, HOSPITALS ARE NOT, NOT,

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.069
AND NOR SHOULD THEY BE STORAGE

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.971
FACILITIES FOR PERSONAL
PROPERTY,

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.040
UM, ESPECIALLY WEAPONS.

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:02.742
OUR HOSPITALS WANT TO ENSURE
THAT OUR PATIENTS

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.510
CAN FREELY ACCESS THE HOSPITAL
SERVICES

00:09:04.577 --> 00:09:06.312
WITHOUT THE CHILLING EFFECT
OF METAL

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:08.147
THAT A METAL DETECTOR MAY CAUSE.

00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:09.582
FURTHER, WE WANT TO ENSURE THAT
OUR

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:11.183
HOSPITALS ARE NOT CONFISCATING

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.351
PERSONAL PROPERTY OF THOSE

00:09:12.418 --> 00:09:13.786
EXPERIENCING HOMELESSNESS,

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:15.187
NOR DO WE WANT TO HAVE TO ENGAGE

