00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:13.465
WHO IS A SPONSOR OF THE BILL
TO ENSURE

00:22:13.532 --> 00:22:15.634
PUBLIC SECTOR LABOR UNIONS
FUNCTION AS GUARANTEED

00:22:15.701 --> 00:22:17.936
BY CALIFORNIA'S COLLECTIVE
BARGAINING LAWS.

00:22:18.003 --> 00:22:20.338
UNION MEMBERS MUST BE ASSURED
THAT WHAT THEY TELL

00:22:20.405 --> 00:22:22.307
THEIR UNION REPRESENTATIVES IN
CONFIDENCE

00:22:22.374 --> 00:22:24.176
CANNOT BE FORCED OUT OF THEIR
REPRESENTATIVES

00:22:24.242 --> 00:22:24.810
BY GOVERNMENT,

00:22:24.876 --> 00:22:26.611
EMPLOYERS OR THEIR AGENTS.

00:22:26.678 --> 00:22:28.680
UNION MEMBERS MUST KNOW AND BE
SECURE

00:22:28.747 --> 00:22:30.348
IN FEELING THAT UNION
REPRESENTATIVES

00:22:30.415 --> 00:22:32.751
WILL NOT BE TRANSFORMED INTO
UNWILLING

00:22:32.818 --> 00:22:34.686
AGENTS OF THE EMPLOYER.

00:22:34.753 --> 00:22:37.456
AB 2421 ACCOMPLISHES THESE
OBJECTIVES

00:22:37.522 --> 00:22:39.458
AND ALIGNS WITH EXISTING
PRECEDENT

00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:40.926
OF THE CALIFORNIA PUBLIC
EMPLOYMENT

00:22:40.992 --> 00:22:43.128
RELATIONS BOARD, OR PERB.

00:22:43.195 --> 00:22:45.664
PERB IS HELD THAT QUESTIONING
UNION

00:22:45.731 --> 00:22:47.499
MEMBERS OR UNION REPRESENTATIVES

00:22:47.566 --> 00:22:51.603
ABOUT UNION ACTIVITIES OR
REPRESENTATION UNLAWFULLY

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:53.138
INTERFERES WITH THE RIGHTS OF

00:22:53.205 --> 00:22:54.439
THE UNION MEMBERS AND THE PUBLIC

00:22:54.506 --> 00:22:56.374
SECTOR UNIONS AND CONSTITUTES

00:22:56.441 --> 00:22:58.110
AN UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICE.

00:22:58.176 --> 00:23:01.146
AB 2421 WOULD MAKE CLEAR THAT
SUCH INTERFERENCE

00:23:01.213 --> 00:23:02.314
WITH UNION REPRESENTATION

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:04.349
BY PUBLIC EMPLOYERS IS UNLAWFUL

00:23:04.416 --> 00:23:06.318
AND AN UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICE.

00:23:06.384 --> 00:23:08.720
THE BILL DOES NOT PROHIBIT
EMPLOYERS

00:23:09.221 --> 00:23:10.822
FROM QUESTIONING EMPLOYEES,

00:23:10.889 --> 00:23:14.126
OR FROM PROHIBIT EMPLOYEES FROM
VOLUNTEERING

00:23:14.192 --> 00:23:16.661
OR SHARING INFORMATION ABOUT
WORKPLACE SAFETY

00:23:16.728 --> 00:23:18.930
OR PROBLEMATIC CONDUCT IN THE
WORKPLACE.

00:23:18.997 --> 00:23:20.799
EMPLOYEES REMAIN FREE TO
VOLUNTARILY

00:23:20.866 --> 00:23:22.534
SHARE ANY SUCH INFORMATION

00:23:22.601 --> 00:23:24.603
WITH THE EMPLOYERS IF THEY
CHOOSE TO DO SO.

00:23:24.669 --> 00:23:27.272
BUT WHAT EMPLOYERS CANNOT DO
IS QUESTION

00:23:27.339 --> 00:23:29.808
THE UNION EMPLOYEE OR THE UNION
REPRESENTATIVE

00:23:29.875 --> 00:23:32.077
ABOUT CONFIDENTIAL
COMMUNICATIONS RELATING

00:23:32.144 --> 00:23:35.046
SPECIFICALLY TO THE
REPRESENTATION.

00:23:37.082 --> 00:23:40.018
WE, PERAK AMENDED THIS BILL ON
OUR OWN TO

00:23:40.085 --> 00:23:41.887
MAKE CLEAR THAT THE
CONFIDENTIALITY DOES

00:23:41.953 --> 00:23:43.922
NOT APPLY TO COMMUNICATIONS
BETWEEN UNION

00:23:43.989 --> 00:23:45.490
MEMBERS AND UNION
REPRESENTATIVES,

00:23:45.557 --> 00:23:47.526
WHO ARE THEMSELVES WITNESSES TO

00:23:47.592 --> 00:23:48.794
OR INVOLVED IN THE EVENTS,

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:50.262
GIVING RISE TO THE
ADMINISTRATIVE,

00:23:50.328 --> 00:23:52.597
DISCIPLINARY OR CRIMINAL
INVESTIGATIONS

00:23:52.664 --> 00:23:53.665
OF UNION MEMBERS.

00:23:53.732 --> 00:23:55.467
WE BELIEVE THAT ELIMINATES THE
CONCERN

00:23:55.534 --> 00:23:57.202
THAT WAS PREVIOUSLY EXPRESSED,

00:23:57.269 --> 00:23:59.070
BUT QUESTIONING A UNION
REPRESENTATIVE

00:23:59.137 --> 00:24:00.105
WHOSE ONLY ROLE IN

00:24:00.172 --> 00:24:01.706
THE MATTER IS FROM THEIR STATUS

00:24:01.773 --> 00:24:02.841
AS A UNION REPRESENTATIVE,

00:24:02.908 --> 00:24:04.810
SERVES NO PURPOSE EXCEPT TO

00:24:04.876 --> 00:24:06.411
FISH FOR UNION STRATEGIES

00:24:06.478 --> 00:24:08.346
AND POSSIBLE EMPLOYEE
CONFESSIONS,

00:24:08.413 --> 00:24:10.682
AND TURN THE UNION
REPRESENTATIVE INTO A WITNESS

00:24:10.749 --> 00:24:12.350
AGAINST THE UNION AND ITS
MEMBERS.

00:24:12.417 --> 00:24:14.486
SUCH CONDUCT INTERFERES WITH
THE BASIC

00:24:14.553 --> 00:24:16.454
AND IMPORTANT FUNCTION OF LABOR
ORGANIZATIONS,

00:24:16.521 --> 00:24:17.923
WHICH IS TO PROVIDE ADVICE

00:24:17.989 --> 00:24:19.724
AND COUNSEL TO MEMBERS REGARDING

00:24:19.791 --> 00:24:21.960
MATTERS WITHIN THE SCOPE OF
REPRESENTATION.

00:24:22.027 --> 00:24:25.797
AB 2421 SENSIBLY PREVENTS SUCH
INTERFERENCE

00:24:25.864 --> 00:24:27.399
WITH UNION REPRESENTATION.

00:24:29.301 --> 00:24:30.869
IS THERE ANOTHER WITNESS?

00:24:30.936 --> 00:24:31.603
OKAY.

00:24:31.670 --> 00:24:32.370
NO WITNESS.

00:24:32.437 --> 00:24:34.239
SO NOW WE'LL JUST GO TO SUPPORT.

00:24:34.306 --> 00:24:34.506
OH.

00:24:34.573 --> 00:24:34.940
YOU ARE.

00:24:35.006 --> 00:24:35.373
OH, NO.

00:24:35.440 --> 00:24:35.707
OH.

00:24:35.774 --> 00:24:36.208
I'M JUST.

00:24:36.274 --> 00:24:37.008
PLEASE JUST SUPPORT.

00:24:37.075 --> 00:24:37.809
OKAY.

00:24:37.876 --> 00:24:39.010
PAT MORAN, AARON READING
ASSOCIATES,

00:24:39.077 --> 00:24:41.012
WE REPRESENT THE PEACE OFFICERS
RESEARCH ASSOCIATION

00:24:41.079 --> 00:24:42.314
OF CALIFORNIA AS CO SPONSORING

00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:43.114
THE BILL AT CALIFORNIA

00:24:43.181 --> 00:24:44.983
ASSOCIATION OF HIGHWAY
PATROLMEN.

00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:47.719
ALSO CO-SPONSORING THE BILL, THE
ORANGE COUNTY

00:24:47.786 --> 00:24:49.654
EMPLOYEES ASSOCIATION IN STRONG
SUPPORT

00:24:49.721 --> 00:24:52.023
AND THE CALIFORNIA ASSOCIATION
OF PROFESSIONAL

00:24:52.090 --> 00:24:55.393
SCIENTISTS UAW 1115, IN SUPPORT
AS WELL.

00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:57.162
THANK YOU, THANK YOU.

00:24:58.330 --> 00:25:00.465
&GT;&GT; MADAM CHAIR, MATT BRAUDE HERE
FOR THE CALIFORNIA

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:02.367
SCHOOL EMPLOYEES ASSOCIATION
AND SUPPORT.

00:25:02.434 --> 00:25:03.568
THANK YOU, THANK YOU.

00:25:04.736 --> 00:25:07.172
ANYONE ELSE SPEAKING IN SUPPORT
OF THE BILL?

00:25:08.273 --> 00:25:09.474
OKAY, WE'LL MOVE TO OPPOSITION.

00:25:09.541 --> 00:25:11.276
OR IS THERE AN OPPOSITION
WITNESS?

00:25:12.744 --> 00:25:13.945
YOU HAVE TWO MINUTES.

00:25:14.012 --> 00:25:14.846
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU.

00:25:14.913 --> 00:25:16.081
SARAH DUQUETTE, ON BEHALF OF
THE RURAL

00:25:16.147 --> 00:25:17.849
COUNTY REPRESENTATIVES OF
CALIFORNIA.

00:25:17.916 --> 00:25:20.051
WHILE WE APPRECIATE THE EFFORTS
TO ADDRESS CONCERNS,

00:25:20.118 --> 00:25:21.653
THE BILL WILL INTERFERE WITH
OUR ABILITY

00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:23.154
TO ENSURE A SAFE WORKPLACE,

00:25:23.221 --> 00:25:24.990
EVEN WITH THE CHANGES TO THE
INTENT LANGUAGE,

00:25:25.056 --> 00:25:26.124
THE SUBSTANTIVE PROVISIONS

00:25:26.191 --> 00:25:27.259
OF THE BILL REMAIN LARGELY

00:25:27.325 --> 00:25:29.527
UNCHANGED AND WILL FUNCTION LIKE
A PRIVILEGE.

00:25:29.594 --> 00:25:31.329
WHILE THE AMENDMENTS ASSERT THAT
THIS ACT

00:25:31.396 --> 00:25:33.164
DOES NOT CREATE AN EVIDENTIARY
PRIVILEGE,

00:25:33.231 --> 00:25:34.666
HOW THE PROVISIONS MIGHT
INTERACT

00:25:34.733 --> 00:25:35.834
WITH JUDICIAL AND ADMINISTRATIVE

00:25:35.901 --> 00:25:38.270
PROCEDURE PROCEEDINGS IS DEEPLY
UNCLEAR.

00:25:38.336 --> 00:25:40.739
AT BEST, IT COULD EASILY BE
INTERPRETED

00:25:40.805 --> 00:25:42.574
IN CIVIL LITIGATION THAT THIRD
PARTIES,

00:25:42.641 --> 00:25:44.376
I.E., THE PLAINTIFF SUING AN
AGENCY,

00:25:44.442 --> 00:25:46.411
CAN COMPEL ACCESS TO THIS
INFORMATION,

00:25:46.478 --> 00:25:47.913
BUT THE AGENCY ITSELF CANNOT

00:25:47.979 --> 00:25:49.848
COMPEL ACCESS TO OR DISCLOSE OF

00:25:49.915 --> 00:25:51.583
THE INFORMATION IN ITS DEFENSE.

00:25:51.650 --> 00:25:53.685
IN ADDITION, AMENDMENTS TO
ADDRESS AN EXCEPTION

00:25:53.752 --> 00:25:55.186
FOR WHEN THE EMPLOYEE
REPRESENTATIVE IS

00:25:55.253 --> 00:25:57.656
A WITNESS OR PARTY TO ANY OF THE
EVENTS FORMING

00:25:57.722 --> 00:25:59.291
THE BASIS OF POTENTIAL
ADMINISTRATIVE,

00:25:59.357 --> 00:26:01.493
DISCIPLINARY OR CRIMINAL
INVESTIGATION

00:26:01.559 --> 00:26:02.727
ARE EXCEPTIONALLY NARROW.

00:26:02.794 --> 00:26:04.863
TO BE CLEAR, THIS IS NOT A
COMPLETE EXEMPTION

00:26:04.930 --> 00:26:06.398
FOR CRIMINAL INVESTIGATIONS.

00:26:06.464 --> 00:26:07.632
RATHER, IT APPLIES ONLY WHEN

00:26:07.699 --> 00:26:08.633
THE EMPLOYEE REPRESENTATIVE

00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:11.736
THEMSELVES WAS A WITNESS OR
PARTY TO AN EVENT.

00:26:11.803 --> 00:26:13.705
IT DOES NOT COVER THE LIKELY
SCENARIO IN WHICH

00:26:13.772 --> 00:26:15.607
AN EMPLOYEE WHO WAS A WITNESS
OR PARTY,

00:26:15.674 --> 00:26:17.976
OR PERPETRATOR OR VICTIM,
PROVIDES RELEVANT

00:26:18.043 --> 00:26:19.411
INFORMATION TO THE
REPRESENTATIVE.

00:26:19.477 --> 00:26:21.046
THIS IS BOTH PROBLEMATIC FOR
CRIMINAL

00:26:21.112 --> 00:26:22.747
AND ADMINISTRATIVE
INVESTIGATIONS.

00:26:22.814 --> 00:26:24.649
WE'RE ALSO CONCERNED HOW THIS
BILL INTERACTS

00:26:24.716 --> 00:26:27.352
WITH RECENTLY ENACTED SB 553
COURTESY,

00:26:27.419 --> 00:26:29.554
WHICH PROVIDES A NEW STRUCTURE
AND REQUIREMENTS FOR

00:26:29.621 --> 00:26:32.190
PREVENTING AND INVESTIGATING
WORKPLACE VIOLENCE.

00:26:32.257 --> 00:26:33.625
IF THE EMPLOYER IS LIMITED IN
ITS

00:26:33.692 --> 00:26:34.926
COMMUNICATIONS WITH EMPLOYEES,

00:26:34.993 --> 00:26:36.294
IT WILL MAKE IT MUCH MORE
DIFFICULT TO

00:26:36.361 --> 00:26:37.929
COMPLY WITH THESE LEGAL
OBLIGATIONS.

00:26:37.996 --> 00:26:39.564
TO CREATE A SAFE WORKPLACE
SHOULD

00:26:39.631 --> 00:26:40.699
ALSO BE NOTED THAT SB

00:26:40.765 --> 00:26:43.101
553 WILL ALLOW COLLECTIVE
BARGAINING REPRESENTATIVES

00:26:43.168 --> 00:26:45.203
STANDING TO SEEK TEMPORARY
RESTRAINING ORDERS

00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.272
IN CONNECTION WITH WORKPLACE
VIOLENCE.

00:26:47.339 --> 00:26:49.574
AB 2400 21ST MAY CREATE A
PROBLEMATIC

00:26:49.641 --> 00:26:50.642
SCENARIO WHEREIN

00:26:50.709 --> 00:26:52.677
SUCH A TRO MAY BE SOUGHT BY AN
EMPLOYER,

00:26:52.744 --> 00:26:54.446
MAY NOT BE ABLE TO FULLY
INVESTIGATE

00:26:54.512 --> 00:26:55.847
THE UNDERLYING FACTS.

00:26:55.914 --> 00:26:57.482
IN CONCLUSION, EVEN AS AMENDED,

00:26:57.549 --> 00:26:59.617
AB 2421 WOULD INTERFERE WITH

00:26:59.684 --> 00:27:01.152
THE PUBLIC EMPLOYER'S
RESPONSIBILITY

00:27:01.219 --> 00:27:01.820
TO PROVIDE A SAFE

00:27:01.886 --> 00:27:03.254
WORKPLACE BY IMPEDING THEIR

00:27:03.321 --> 00:27:04.356
ABILITY TO COMMUNICATE WITH

