00:31:43.501 --> 00:31:45.303
THEIR SCHEDULES, WORK LOCATIONS,

00:31:45.370 --> 00:31:46.604
COLLECTIVE BARGAINING UNIT,

00:31:46.671 --> 00:31:48.773
OR AMONG OTHER LOGICAL WORK
RELATED

00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:50.041
GROUPINGS FOR THE PURPOSES

00:31:50.108 --> 00:31:53.244
OF THE CALCULATION OF
PENSIONABLE COMPENSATION.

00:31:53.311 --> 00:31:54.879
THE RETIREMENT SYSTEM FOR PUBLIC

00:31:54.946 --> 00:31:56.147
EMPLOYEES IN CALIFORNIA

00:31:56.214 --> 00:31:59.017
OPERATES UNDER TWO DISTINCT
PROVISIONS

00:31:59.083 --> 00:32:02.053
EITHER THE PUBLIC EMPLOYMENT
RETIREMENT LAW OR

00:32:02.120 --> 00:32:06.291
THE COUNTY EMPLOYMENT RETIREMENT
LAW OF 1937.

00:32:06.357 --> 00:32:09.160
SARAH SEARLE GOVERNS RETIREMENT
SYSTEMS

00:32:09.227 --> 00:32:11.462
FOR COUNTY AND DISTRICT
EMPLOYEES UNDER

00:32:11.796 --> 00:32:14.032
PENSIONABLE COMPENSATION IS
DEFINED

00:32:14.098 --> 00:32:16.167
AS THE AVERAGE COMPENSATION UPON

00:32:16.234 --> 00:32:19.170
THE BASIS OF THE AVERAGE NUMBER
OF DAYS ORDINARILY

00:32:19.237 --> 00:32:21.606
WORKED BY PERSONS IN THE SAME
GRADE,

00:32:21.673 --> 00:32:24.142
CLASS, OR POSITIONS DURING THE
PERIOD,

00:32:24.208 --> 00:32:26.344
OR AT THE SAME RATE OF PAY.

00:32:26.411 --> 00:32:28.946
PEARL OVERSEES THE
ADMINISTRATION

00:32:29.013 --> 00:32:29.914
OF CALPERS FOR

00:32:29.981 --> 00:32:31.449
THE EMPLOYEES FOR BOTH STATE

00:32:31.516 --> 00:32:33.151
AND LOCAL JURISDICTIONS.

00:32:33.217 --> 00:32:36.487
THIS GROUP PROVIDES A CLEAR
DEFINITION OF GROUP

00:32:36.554 --> 00:32:39.057
OR CLASS EMPLOYMENT UTILIZED
AS PART

00:32:39.324 --> 00:32:42.060
OF ITS DEFINITION OF PENSIONABLE
COMPENSATION,

00:32:42.126 --> 00:32:43.895
WHEREAS SARAH, ON THE OTHER
HAND,

00:32:43.961 --> 00:32:46.264
THIS DOES NOT PROVIDE A CLEAR

00:32:46.331 --> 00:32:47.465
DEFINITION FOR THAT PORTION

00:32:47.532 --> 00:32:50.201
OF THEIR PROVISIONS OF
PENSIONABLE COMPENSATION,

00:32:50.268 --> 00:32:52.670
INTRODUCING WHAT WE WOULD KNOW
AS AMBIGUITY

00:32:52.737 --> 00:32:54.639
AND POTENTIAL DISPARITIES.

00:32:54.706 --> 00:32:57.608
THIS AMBIGUITY IS WHAT
COMPENSATION

00:32:57.675 --> 00:32:59.043
ITEMS ARE PENSIONABLE

00:32:59.110 --> 00:33:01.446
THAT CAN LEAD TO REDUCED
RETIREMENTS.

00:33:01.512 --> 00:33:05.249
SO AB 2284 ADDRESSES THIS
INCONSISTENCY AND WILL

00:33:05.316 --> 00:33:07.652
PROVIDE CLARITY FOR THE COUNTY
RETIREMENT

00:33:07.719 --> 00:33:10.188
SYSTEM BY CREATING A DEFINITION
FOR AND I QUOTE

00:33:10.254 --> 00:33:12.623
GRADE SIMILAR TO ONE FOUND IN
PEARL.

00:33:12.690 --> 00:33:15.493
FOR THE TERM GROUP, THE
CONSISTENCY

00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:17.095
WILL REDUCE THE LEGAL BURDENS

00:33:17.161 --> 00:33:19.564
FOR ALL PARTIES AS WELL AS ALLOW

00:33:19.630 --> 00:33:21.232
FOR SECURE RETIREMENTS.

00:33:21.299 --> 00:33:22.900
SO I WOULD LIKE TO EMPHASIZE
THAT THIS

00:33:22.967 --> 00:33:26.504
BILL IS PERMISSIVE AND IN
NATURE,

00:33:26.571 --> 00:33:28.773
AND DOES NOT RESTRICT RETIREMENT
SYSTEMS

00:33:28.840 --> 00:33:30.641
FROM MAKING THEIR OWN DECISIONS.

00:33:30.708 --> 00:33:32.410
THEY CAN STILL MAKE THEIR OWN
DECISIONS.

00:33:32.477 --> 00:33:34.579
SO WITH THAT, THROUGH THE CHAIR,

00:33:34.645 --> 00:33:36.114
